const craft={
 ultragui:['Map tasks to screens and states before drawing controls. Make primary actions discoverable, keep information needed for a decision close to that decision, and use progressive disclosure for advanced options. Define density, type hierarchy, alignment and semantic color as reusable tokens. A small icon and a large hit target can coexist; distinguish the visual glyph from input bounds. Prefer clear labels over unexplained tiny symbols.', 'Prototype the actual hardest state: a long name, large inventory, offline response, small viewport or modal over gameplay. Use one focus owner and predictable back/cancel behavior. Bind data and errors before polishing surfaces. Review screenshots at actual scale, but also click, scroll and traverse the working screen. Gradients, shadows and animated borders cannot repair a broken information hierarchy.'],
 ultraanimation:['Write the action as intention, anticipation, contact/action, follow-through and recovery. Identify weight, support foot, center of mass, line of action and silhouette for each key pose. Block poses and timing before adding interpolation; use arcs and spacing to communicate acceleration rather than smoothing every curve equally. Choose how exaggeration serves the style and camera, and preserve readable holds for important gameplay cues.', 'Inspect deformation, foot planting, hand contacts and root trajectory at the actual playback speed and slowed down. Design interruption from every action state, including loss of target or owner. Tune transitions against movement speed and input latency rather than isolated clip beauty. Check repeated playback and extremes, then reconnect audio/VFX only after contact timing is stable. Keep editable rig/clip sources and verified import settings.'],
 ultravfx:['Define what the effect tells the player, its important moment and the camera distance. Start with a readable silhouette/value core, then add supporting motion and a short decay. Describe emission shape, direction, scale, lifetime, timing curves and color evolution explicitly. Coordinate anticipation/impact/recovery with animation while keeping damage independent of particles. Reserve visual intensity for meaningful events instead of making every layer bright.', 'Inspect single trigger, overlapping triggers and worst-case screen coverage against a real background. Check front/back readability, camera occlusion, depth sorting, bounds and exposure. Cap emitters, transparent layers, lights and lifetime; choose quality tiers deliberately. Implement cancellation and complete teardown, then test owner despawn, scene change and interrupted playback. Read actual performance evidence rather than calling an emitter cheap because its count looks small.'],
 ultramodelling:['Define scale, use, camera distance, style and deformation before choosing topology. Solve silhouette with primary masses, establish secondary forms and reserve small detail for visible or functional regions. Use orthographic/perspective references as evidence, not blindly matched photographs with lens distortion. Keep pivots and modular snap points intentional. Plan hard/soft edges, UV seams and material breaks together so shading and texturing reinforce form.', 'Use editable topology and a restrained modifier stack. Spend density on silhouette and deformation, then inspect normals, skinning extremes and material response. Maintain consistent texel density, texture channels and source files. Create collision/LOD only when required by use and target. Export one representative asset early, reimport it and verify axes, dimensions, pivot, texture paths and actions before scaling production to many assets.'],
 ultraworld:['Map the player journey from spawn through goal, challenge, recovery and return. Derive route widths, jump spans and sightlines from the real controller/camera rather than decoration scale. Block out a complete route and test circulation before dressing it. Use landmarks, contrast and framing to guide without saturating the world with arrows. Vary pressure and rest, preserve readable paths and provide recovery from foreseeable falls or missed interactions.', 'Define a modular kit with coherent dimensions, pivots, trim/material usage and collision. Dress by focal importance and repeated visual rhythm; break repetition intentionally with landmarks rather than random scatter. Match lighting, atmosphere and props to one style sheet. Test traversal at player eye level, alternate routes, spawn/reset and streaming/load boundaries. Capture routes as well as still compositions; a beautiful room that traps the controller is unfinished.'],
 ultragameplay:['Create a small state/transition table with input, preconditions, committed result, feedback, interruption and recovery. Define timing windows in units appropriate to simulation rather than arbitrary render frames. Separate configuration, simulation and presentation; keep one authority for each consequential value. Tune one complete interaction loop first, including the expected failure and retry, before multiplying abilities or content.', 'Evaluate feel through actual input-to-response behavior, not only source review. Check held/rapid input, target loss, simultaneous actions, low frame rate, reset and death. Trace cleanup and cooldown ownership. Integrate UI/audio/animation/VFX with domain events and prevent duplicate state transitions. For multiplayer, compare local responsiveness with server validation and explicitly test duplicate, delayed and rejected actions.'],
 ultraaudio:['Build an event-to-sound map with purpose, priority, spatial behavior and lifetime. Establish a gain hierarchy and frequency roles so feedback remains intelligible under gameplay density. Choose actual licensed sources and preserve editable project/stems where available. Align transients to verified action/contact timing; add controlled variation to repeated events without randomizing away meaningful information.', 'Test the actual mix at quiet, typical and worst-case density with mute/volume controls and scene transitions. Check looping seams, clipping, listener placement, attenuation and overlap limits. Critical cues need a usable visual or other alternative. Cap voice ownership and stop sounds on cancellation/despawn. Report listening tests separately from waveform/export checks, and label untested output devices.'],
 ultranetwork:['Write a sender/validator/commit/receiver map for each consequential action. Bound message size, rate, lifetime and authority checks. Give repeatable requests an idempotency story and uncertain delivery a visible recovery state. Never let a cosmetic event, model assertion or transport acknowledgement mutate authoritative inventory, purchases or saves without the owning system committing it.', 'Exercise malformed, duplicate, delayed and reordered input, interrupted sessions and reconnect. Confirm state convergence through read-back on the authoritative side. Separate retry-safe reads from writes with uncertain outcomes, and respect actual provider/service quotas. Document schema migrations and conflict behavior. A successful single-client test cannot establish multiplayer correctness under latency.'],
 ultraperformance:['Build a representative scene/workload with a stable measurement window, target device/tier and fixed quality settings. Record startup, steady state, spikes and sustained use. Separate CPU, GPU, I/O, allocations and networking before choosing a fix. Write the expected causal effect and a rollback point; avoid accumulating unrelated speculative optimizations.', 'Optimize the measured dominant cost and repeat the same workload. Track frame-time distributions, memory growth and input responsiveness where available. Consider culling, batching, lifetime cleanup, work frequency and quality tiers without breaking correctness. Verify cache invalidation, pooling resets and unload/reload. Report measured changes with conditions and raw evidence; retain hypotheses as hypotheses when profiling access is missing.'],
 ultraengineering:['Trace the complete request through UI, configuration, transport, handler, state mutation and returned result. Keep public contracts and persisted formats explicit. Read callers before changing a helper and resolve dependencies before adding another package. Implement one complete path with bounded queues/timeouts and defined cancellation; handle errors at the layer that owns recovery.', 'Plan upgrade and rollback alongside the new feature. Preserve unknown settings and user data, maintain stable identities and fail visibly when a migration cannot safely continue. Verify the final package as well as source. Distinguish authored code, build success, runtime read-back and external service coverage. Avoid hidden automation, arbitrary command surfaces and unbounded retries.'],
 ultraaccessibility:['Define the device/input matrix and identify essential information available only through color, motion, sound, hover or precision. Build keyboard/controller/touch alternatives using the target’s native semantics and focus model. Make target area, text scaling, safe areas and scroll behavior part of layout rather than late patches. Honor reduced motion and user preferences for newly created elements too.', 'Run the primary flow without a mouse, then test the supported other inputs and larger text. Inspect painted contrast, focus visibility/return, modal escape and disabled/hidden controls. Test long localized strings and narrow displays with real content. Keep announcements useful and bounded. Explain actual device/assistive coverage and unresolved barriers instead of labeling an unchecked screen universally accessible.'],
 ultraqa:['Define an acceptance matrix that can expose a false positive: trigger, expected state, actual state, evidence and environment. Separate authored files, successful transport, applied tool result, observed running behavior and whole-task completion. Reproduce the first concrete failure, inspect adjacent state ownership and use diagnostics that preserve privacy and drafts.', 'Exercise cancellation, remount/navigation, concurrent actions, permission changes, stale results and timeouts where relevant. Keep unfinished checks visible in the task plan; a green tool chip is only that tool’s result. Reuse still-valid evidence and rerun affected paths after changes. Verify the shipped artifact and maintain clear local-fixture, authenticated-provider, native-editor and physical-device boundaries.']
};
function engineIds(context={}){const raw=context.engines||[];return [...new Set(raw.map(x=>String(x).toLowerCase()).map(x=>['software','code','desktop'].includes(x)?'workspace':x).filter(x=>engines[x]))];}
